WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.760
And I want to take up in June the 6th, 1923, in Volume 15.

2
00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:17.160
We began a little bit of it last week, but I want to do the whole thing.

3
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:20.040
And here we're talking about our desires.

4
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.120
The heading says the sign that the soul is all for God is actually has a taste for nothing

5
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.120
but him.

6
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.240
That means she desires nothing but him.

7
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.940
So put the word desire there.

8
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:38.560
And before we even start, I want to give you Sam 10, 3, Sam 21, 2, you probably have

9
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.360
this from last week.

10
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:48.600
I have to do it for the recording though, Sam 38 verse 9, Sam 40 verses 6 to 8.

11
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:54.440
So Louisa said, "I was concerned about the reason why my Jesus wasn't coming, and I said

12
00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:58.160
to myself, 'Who knows what evil there is in my interior.'

13
00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:05.400
Now, she's kept that up for 15 volumes regardless of the fact of what Jesus has told her."

14
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.800
And so that he hides himself so as not to be displeased.

15
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.920
Now, this hiding of himself, I want to give you a new reference there.

16
00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:17.880
And that's Luke 17, 21, "The kingdom of God is within you.

17
00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.400
Where would you look for him?

18
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.800
He is within."

19
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:29.040
So he, moving in my interior, told me, my daughter, the sign that there's nothing evil

20
00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:37.160
and that the interior of the soul is completely, not as completely filled with God is that

21
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:41.880
nothing is left for her which is not all mine.

22
00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:42.880
Okay?

23
00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:47.960
Now, what he's doing is he's giving us a bit of discernment to find out if we have in fact

24
00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:51.120
filled ourselves completely with God.

25
00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:57.840
And that is, there would be nothing left to her except what is his.

26
00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:04.240
And that in everything that may happen inside and outside of her, she no longer desires

27
00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.840
anything.

28
00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:10.120
Her desire is only for the Lord and from him.

29
00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:15.960
Now, I've changed that into desire for you because it makes sense, doesn't it?

30
00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:21.000
And not only with profane and in different things, but also with holy things, pious people,

31
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:27.320
I love that, services, music and everything because you can go to mass or any religious

32
00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:31.600
service for a completely selfish thing that you want to save your own soul.

33
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.720
And you mightn't be going to give any glory to God.

34
00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:42.680
And you mightn't be going to praise and worship him and to love your neighbor as yourself.

35
00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:47.000
So he said, "Everything is cold and indifferent to her.

36
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.360
All this stuff that impresses everybody else."

37
00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:53.520
And like something that does not belong to her.

38
00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.360
And the reason is natural.

39
00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:01.680
If the soul is completely filled with the Lord, she's also filled with his desires.

40
00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:07.560
Now, if you get filled with his desires, you will be very interested in his church and

41
00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:12.960
you will be very interested in his people and you will be very interested in spreading

42
00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:18.080
his word and his life so that the people are saved.

43
00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:27.000
Because one Timothy, I think it's three, I'm not sure, God wants everyone to be saved

44
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.760
and come to the knowledge of the truth.

45
00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:37.520
So he says, "My desire is hers and other desires find no place in which to put themselves."

46
00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:42.600
I gave you the song of songs, "My beloved is mine and I am his.

47
00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.320
His desire is for me and mine is for him."

48
00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:50.800
That's a song of songs 7, 10, you have that one, haven't you?

49
00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:56.640
"Therefore, as beautiful as they may be, they hold no attraction for this soul.

50
00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.120
Rather, they are as though dead for her."

51
00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.000
So let's put it this way.

52
00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.880
Other people will spend hours watching the television, entertaining themselves with all

53
00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:08.920
kinds of junk, "I couldn't get myself to turn it on."

54
00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:09.920
Why?

55
00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.440
It's a different planet, it's a different world, it's not where you're living.

56
00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.120
It's not the level that you're living at.

57
00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:19.880
You're not going to find an eagle scratching the ground looking for something on the ground,

58
00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:20.880
are you?

59
00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:24.480
No, no, they're the seagulls and they make a fierce amount of noise.

60
00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:29.360
Whereas the eagle takes to the skies, you know, and the Lord has called us to be eagles

61
00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:32.040
spiritually so you have to take to the skies.

62
00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.680
So I gave you references for that, didn't I?

63
00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.320
Now let's come to the next paragraph.

64
00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:42.000
On the other hand, this is very Jewish, on the one hand and on the other hand, you know?

65
00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:47.560
On the other hand, the soul who is not completely mine is empty.

66
00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:53.240
Now notice there's only two things given to you here, you're either full or you're empty.

67
00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:58.520
Now notice the Lord doesn't accept the fact that I could be half full.

68
00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:04.520
Because if I'm half full, the other half has junk that he's not interested in.

69
00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:09.840
So as far as he's concerned, you're either full or empty of him.

70
00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:14.840
And as things surround her, she feels as many desires within herself if those are things

71
00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.600
which she likes.

72
00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:21.800
If on the other hand they are things she doesn't like, she feels disgust for them.

73
00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:27.720
And so she's in a continuous alteration of desire and disgust.

74
00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:32.040
That's typical of the way people live, isn't it?

75
00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:38.020
And since any desire of which doesn't come from me is not lasting, they're really hot

76
00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:41.240
about something today and cold about it tomorrow.

77
00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:45.080
Many times desires turn into disgusts.

78
00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:49.720
And this is why many variations in character are noticed.

79
00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:55.120
At one stage the person is really interested in serving the neighbor and the next thing

80
00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.520
they're not even interested in the neighbor's name.

81
00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.080
So the variations in character.

82
00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:03.720
At one stage they're too sad or they're too cheerful.

83
00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:07.440
In other words, they're down too much or they're up too much.

84
00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:11.640
They're all irascible, you can't touch them, they're like porcupines.

85
00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:14.680
And another time they're all affable, they're all friendly.

86
00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.880
So there's too much variation there.

87
00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:21.080
And this is volume 15 and you have to remember all the things that have been told to you

88
00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:27.320
up to now and that is that the soul who is in God must be stable.

89
00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:35.880
They must continue in their love and service of God to himself and to their neighbors with

90
00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:38.240
no variation.

91
00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:43.800
That there's actually a continuous praise and glory to God and continuous love and service

92
00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:48.480
for him as well.

93
00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:54.320
So it is the void of me, now we're talking about the ones who are not desiring the Lord.

94
00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:59.480
It's the void of me that she has in her soul and gives her so many variations in character.

95
00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:03.840
It's nothing similar to mine, for I'm always the same and I never change.

96
00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:09.520
You see the immutability of God and he's been telling us for many volumes that we have

97
00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:16.000
to become like him and therefore the soul becomes very, very stable.

98
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:21.760
So he's going to give us discernment now in the next paragraph and it's all about these

99
00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:23.800
desires.

100
00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:29.560
So kind of who are you and what is shown in what you desire.

101
00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:37.960
So now do you have any desire for what exists down here that's on earth?

102
00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.360
What do you fear?

103
00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:45.880
That there be some evil in you and that because of it displeased I hide myself wherever

104
00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:50.800
I am, Jesus said there cannot be evil.

105
00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:58.400
Now I've given you references for that ad nauseam but first of all I want to give you

106
00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:05.320
the first letter of Saint John chapter 3 verses 2 to 6 that anybody who's truly in God does

107
00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:09.320
not sin.

108
00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:19.760
So I want to give you 1 John 2 verse 6 verse 17 and verses 24 to 29.

109
00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:26.280
I want to give you my usual Hebrews 12, 14, nothing unholy or unworthy can enter the presence

110
00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:28.520
of God.

111
00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:41.560
Isaiah 35 verse 8 on the road that the redeemed are on, those who are unclean cannot join.

112
00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:43.160
There's lots of others as well.

113
00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:46.520
So wherever I am there cannot be evil.

114
00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:53.640
Now from volume 1 the Lord has been telling us that the one thing he hates is sin.

115
00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:58.480
Sin is totally intolerable to him and the reason why we get chastisements is that sin

116
00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:03.240
rises up from the earth and sent right back to us in chastisement.

117
00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:07.240
So wherever I am there can be no sin.

118
00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:12.840
And this is the reason why when we are trying to grow in closeness to God that there will

119
00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:17.560
be continuous purification it doesn't stop.

120
00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:24.000
And we have seen the level of spirituality that Louisa is at and she's still being purified.

121
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:28.800
Okay, it doesn't stop as long as you're breathing on this earth.

122
00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:36.440
He has even used the lovely expression that something made of gold needs to be dusted.

123
00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:41.560
So Louisa said, "My love, I don't feel like getting a desire for anything as good as it

124
00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:42.560
might be."

125
00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:47.840
Now Louisa at this point still doesn't realize that all these teachings are for generations

126
00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:49.840
coming after her.

127
00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:54.160
So she reacts only from her own personal position.

128
00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:59.400
How can I get a taste for other things if the pain of your privation absorbs me, embitters

129
00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:03.720
me down to the marrow of my bones and makes me forget about everything.

130
00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:08.040
And the only thing which is present to me and driven into my heart is the nail that

131
00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.760
I am without you.

132
00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:14.120
So she's saying, "You really got me on this privation thing.

133
00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:16.440
I couldn't possibly think of anything else."

134
00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:21.760
But most other people are not at that level and along with your relationship with God you

135
00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:25.320
might want other things as well.

136
00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:32.680
And Jesus said, "The fact that you only think of me, this tells you that you are mine and

137
00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:39.120
that you are filled with me because every desire has this power.

138
00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:41.520
It is my desire.

139
00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:45.640
If it is my desire, it transforms the creature into me."

140
00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:50.240
It has two Corinthians 3, 18.

141
00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:55.880
That you are transformed into the image that you reflect in contemplation.

142
00:10:55.880 --> 00:11:00.600
And also John 8, 32, it's the truth that sets you free.

143
00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:05.760
And Jesus keeps on making sure that Louisa sees the truth.

144
00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:09.240
Truth is reality as it really is.

145
00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:17.960
And so Jesus keeps on keeping Louisa at this very sharp edge of truth.

146
00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:23.880
So if it is a natural taste, he said, it sweeps you into human things.

147
00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:26.640
The her is the soul.

148
00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:30.480
If it is a desire for passions, it casts her into the current of evil.

149
00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:35.280
It may even seem a desire is something trivial, but it is not so.

150
00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:36.800
Watch this.

151
00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:41.840
The desire is the first act of either good or evil.

152
00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:48.480
That's a very, very important statement that's been made there.

153
00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:50.840
And he's going to illustrate this here.

154
00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:57.840
But I remember years ago, giving a retreat to a community of enclosed sisters.

155
00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:01.440
And there was one particular one who was really willing to share with me.

156
00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:04.600
I said to her, "Look, can I take a risk and ask you a question?"

157
00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:07.800
And I promised I'll never tell anybody who you are or anything else.

158
00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:09.480
And she said, "No, it's okay."

159
00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:14.600
I said, "When you go to confession," now I'm talking about a nun who's been in an enclosed

160
00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:21.400
monastery under solemn vows for years, I couldn't even imagine what she would tell in confession.

161
00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:22.400
Okay.

162
00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:29.040
I said, "When you go to confession, what do you confess?"

163
00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:33.440
Now anybody could say, "Sorry, off limits."

164
00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:34.440
You didn't.

165
00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:35.600
You never even hesitated.

166
00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:39.320
She said, "I confess the first movements."

167
00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:40.920
I said, "Don't tell me anything else.

168
00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:43.320
I know everything you're trying to tell me."

169
00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:46.520
I said, "That's what I wanted."

170
00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:52.280
What she's saying is that you go from the sin and all its roots up here and then you go

171
00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:57.200
down to the roots and you go down and down and then you get to the finest roots where

172
00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:59.880
there's no possibility of any more sin.

173
00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:01.600
That's where she was at.

174
00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:07.120
So that if there was any temptation to anger or anything else, she was picking it up so

175
00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:11.920
completely at the roots, there would never be an expression of it.

176
00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:14.400
It's absolutely incredible.

177
00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:17.240
And that's what Jesus is saying here.

178
00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:24.000
The desire is the first act in either good or evil and he wants to bring us to a level

179
00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:29.000
of holiness whereby you actually deal with the first movements.

180
00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:30.600
Is that okay?

181
00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:33.960
Now watch how he's going to illustrate this in the case of Adam.

182
00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:39.520
And so the next paragraph is he's actually telling us how Adam sinned.

183
00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:48.640
Why did Adam sin, he said, "One, he removed his gaze from the divine attraction and he

184
00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.360
turned it to something else."

185
00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:55.240
It actually doesn't matter what the something else was.

186
00:13:55.240 --> 00:14:02.560
And as Eve presented the fruit to have him eat it, he looked at the fruit.

187
00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:06.940
So once he starts looking at it, the desire is awake.

188
00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:09.400
And his sight took pleasure in looking at it.

189
00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:13.840
His hearing took delight in hearing the words of Eve.

190
00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:17.320
That if he ate the fruit, he would become like God.

191
00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:19.920
And his palate took pleasure in eating it.

192
00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:23.800
So desire was the first act of his ruin.

193
00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:28.280
Now can I give you that in a very simple language for ladies?

194
00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:31.520
I don't know for the gentleman, but for the ladies.

195
00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:34.880
You're going along the street and you're just going about your business.

196
00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:39.520
You're passed by this wonderful shop and you see this magnificent blouse, coat or skirt

197
00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:43.800
or whatever it is that you're like, you don't need it at all.

198
00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:49.080
But when you see it, you can think of ten reasons why you have to buy that.

199
00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:52.120
And it's your eyes have created the desire.

200
00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.560
Does that make sense to you?

201
00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:57.320
That's what she's talking about.

202
00:14:57.320 --> 00:15:02.400
Your eyes are now on an object, which is nothing to do with God.

203
00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:06.520
You know you don't need the darn thing, but you're going to go in and buy it anyway.

204
00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:11.040
Because you say, oh, I'm sure one of my nieces could get married, you know?

205
00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:15.080
Or we could have to go on holidays or we might have to visit their relatives or whatever.

206
00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:16.740
You think of all kinds of reasons.

207
00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:22.080
And all you're trying to do is justify the fact that you're giving in to your desire.

208
00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:25.440
And so I recommend a particular exercise to you.

209
00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:27.920
It actually works a treat.

210
00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:30.640
And that is go to a shopping center.

211
00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:33.240
Well, you probably have to go on business anyway.

212
00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:37.880
And go to one of these clothes shops and stand outside, I've done it, it works.

213
00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:42.000
Thanks be to God, I need nothing.

214
00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.000
And walk on.

215
00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.320
It works a treat.

216
00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:50.920
You've no idea how it liberates you, but you must try it.

217
00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:54.680
Because otherwise you can leave this stuff in theory.

218
00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.640
You see, Jesus is explaining something very simple.

219
00:15:57.640 --> 00:16:01.800
Adam took his eyes off that and put them onto something else.

220
00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:04.160
And therefore began desiring it.

221
00:16:04.160 --> 00:16:06.680
Isn't that it?

222
00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:11.160
All you've got to do is go around into one of these shops.

223
00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:12.480
And there's lots of stuff there.

224
00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:13.480
They're all nice.

225
00:16:13.480 --> 00:16:17.560
Well, some of it's nice anyway, but you don't need to have that.

226
00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:20.280
But you'll come out with a few bags.

227
00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:27.280
Am I wrong or am I right?

228
00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:30.800
I've been asked by a few people, had I gone to a particular store to see it.

229
00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:31.800
I said, no, thanks.

230
00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:35.160
I don't need any more temptations.

231
00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:36.800
